##
#
# 2D scalar conservation equation with the non-convex KPP flux f(u) = (sin
# u, cos u) proposed by Kurganov, Petrova, Popov [1], Section 6.3 (Figure
# 4c) of [2].
#
# The initial data is u_0 = 14 pi / 4 inside the unit disc and u_0 = pi / 4
# otherwise on the domain [-2,2] x [-2.5,1.5] with Dirichlet boundary
# conditions. The solution develops a rotating composite wave that many
# high-order schemes fail to capture. The final time is t = 1.
#
# Greedy wave speed augmented by an entropy inequality for one random
# Kruzkov entropy k = theta u_i + (1 - theta) u_j per pair (i,j) and time
# step, theta uniformly distributed in (0,1) ([2] draws one theta_i per
# grid point and uses k_i = theta_i U_i^min + (1 - theta_i) U_i^max). This
# is the only variant of Figure 4 of [2] that converges to the entropy
# solution.
#
# First-order method (limiter iterations = 0), SSPRK(3,3), CFL = 0.5. [2]
# uses P1 elements on a nonuniform Delaunay mesh with 118850 grid points.
# The chosen 43 x 43 subdivisions with refinement 3 give a uniform Q1 mesh
# with 345^2 = 119025 grid points, so the solutions differ in detail from
# Figure 4 of [2].
#
# Setting "limiter iterations = 2" gives the second-order method. With
# "subdivisions x/y = 1" and refinement level 10 (around 1.05M gridpoints,
# erk 33, CFL 0.9) the high-order computation requires around 320 time
# steps and runs for about (12min / #n_cores) on a modern system.
#
# [1] Kurganov, Petrova, Popov: Adaptive Semidiscrete Central-Upwind
#     Schemes for Nonconvex Hyperbolic Conservation Laws. SIAM Journal on
#     Scientific Computing 2007, vol. 29. DOI 10.1137/040614189.
#
# [2] J.-L. Guermond, M. Maier, B. Popov, L. Saavedra, I. Tomas.
#     First-order greedy invariant-domain preserving approximation for
#     hyperbolic problems: scalar conservation laws, and p-system. J. Sci.
#     Comput., 100:46, 2024. arXiv:2310.01713
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = kpp-random-entropy
  set align time steps  = true
  set tasks             = vtu output
  set final time        = 1.00
  set timer granularity = 1.00
end

subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 2
  set equation  = scalar conservation
  set flux      = kpp
end

subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry        = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement = 3

  subsection rectangular domain
    set position bottom left      = -2, -2.5
    set position top right        =  2,  1.5
    set subdivisions x            = 43
    set subdivisions y            = 43
    set boundary condition bottom = dirichlet
    set boundary condition left   = dirichlet
    set boundary condition right  = dirichlet
    set boundary condition top    = dirichlet
  end
end

subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = function
  set direction     = 1, 0
  set position      = 0, 0

  subsection function
    # pi / 4 = 0.78539816339745
    set expression = 0.78539816339745 * if(x*x + y*y <= 1, 14, 1)
  end
end

subsection F - HyperbolicModule
  subsection limiter
    set iterations = 0
  end

  subsection wave speed estimator
    set use greedy wavespeed = true
    set use averaged entropy = false
    set random entropies     = 1
  end
end

subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.5
  set cfl max               = 0.5
  set cfl recovery strategy = none
  set time stepping scheme  = ssprk 33
end

subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection full
    set vtu output quantities = u
  end
end
